Brief descriptions:

Flip fraction (flip_frac) [Sector]:
    Fraction of energy "flipped" from adjacent sectors due to wind deflection.
    Column: flip_fraction_weighted_by_predicted_power

Speedup gradient (speedup_gradient) [Sector]:
    Max |speedup_current - speedup_neighbour| between adjacent sectors.
    Captures directional speedup variability.

Concentration ratio [Pair]:
    (12 - effective_sectors) / 11, where effective_sectors = 1/SUM(weight^2).
    Measures how concentrated energy is across sectors.

Roughness mismatch [Sector]:
    |log(z0_WTG / z0_MM)| using reference roughness lengths.
    Explored in: Roughness mismatch exploration.py
    Finding: Strong in flat terrain (r=0.47) but absorbed by other features
    in the Bayesian model.

Severity fraction [Pair]:
    |dRIX_0.3| / (|dRIX_0.3| + |dRIX_mild| + eps)
    where dRIX_mild = dRIX_0.0501 - dRIX_0.3
    Measures what fraction of terrain mismatch is in "severe" slopes.

Severity-weighted RIX [Pair]:
    RIX_avg_0.0501_sector * severity_fraction
    Combines terrain complexity with severity concentration.

Slope (dz/distance) [Pair]:
    |dz| / distance_m
    Average slope between the two sites.

Relative RIX [Sector]:
    RIX_sector / (pair_mean_RIX + 0.1)
    Within-pair RIX variation.

Inter-sector k variability (k_sector_std) [Pair]:
    std(k_MM) across all 12 sectors.
    How variable the Weibull shape parameter is across directions.

|dz| (abs_dz) [Pair]:
    |WTG_elevation - MM_elevation|
    Note: Dominant in the EY model (rank #1) but weak for WS.

Log energy weight [Sector]:
    log(weight_energy_predicted + eps)
    Low-energy sectors have higher relative errors.

Speedup mismatch (abs_log_speedup) [Sector]:
    |log(speedup_WTG / speedup_MM)|
    Magnitude of speedup difference.

Deflection mismatch (abs_turning) [Sector]:
    |d_turning_deg|
    Raw deflection magnitude (gradient version is more informative).

Terrain complexity (RIX_avg) [Sector]:
    Average RIX_0.3 between WTG and MM.
    Surprisingly weak -- possibly because terrain effects are captured
    indirectly by speedup, turning, and dRIX features.

Terrain mismatch (abs_dRIX) [Sector]:
    |dRIX_0.3_sector|
    Difference in terrain severity between sites.


